# Club & Grub level file - format 2 (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md 7.11). Chieftains' Pyre: developer level of enemies-C for the
# Rival Chieftains (docs/expansion/PLAN.md P2.3; DESIGN.md B.6, GAMEPLAY.md 13.6): one screen around the pyre, the
# altar of the Great Roast in the middle (one-way) 3 rows over the floor, level with the side ledges (lead designer,
# wf9 G35: no standable surface higher than 3 rows, so a chieftain on it stays clear of the HUD), under a 5-row rock
# crown (ceiling underside 80 px under the room's top, as D9b's w9_l3: no jumping body rises higher), Gorm on the floor and
# Gulla waiting on the altar (solo: he tags in when Gorm falls; a co-op file would have both fight at once). The
# arena's floor edges are the Roc perches of the roast thieves. Its bot graph is resources/bots/test_enemies_chieftain
# .json (core-B's baker), so the chieftains fight on hero physics here; tests/test_enemies_chieftain.gd replays its
# recorded club routes on this file. No special lies here, so a club route never picks one up. Not part of any
# campaign (kind = test).

[meta]
format = 2
id = test_enemies_chieftain
name = "Chieftains' Pyre"
kind = test
book = 2
biome = volcano
terrain_a = volcano/terrain
terrain_b = volcano/terrain_obsidian
background = volcano
music = level_volcano
author = enemies-C
notes = "PLAN.md P2.3: the Rival Chieftains on hero physics (HeroBot) where the level has its bot graph; else the state machine."

